# Bifrost, the LLM gateway for hosted tenants (railway.bifrost.toml).
#
# Tenant daemons never hold our Anthropic key: each pod gets a Bifrost
# virtual key (minted by squelch-control at signup) and sends its unchanged
# Anthropic-wire traffic to this service's /anthropic route. Bifrost holds
# the real provider key, enforces per-tenant dollar budgets, and meters
# usage — the metering the daemon's own ledger is reconciled against.
#
# Wrapped in a Dockerfile rather than deployed straight from the upstream
# image so the pinned version is code-reviewed here, and so an auth proxy
# or baked config has an obvious place to land if the OSS admin plane ever
# needs fronting. Root user for the same reason as Dockerfile.prometheus:
# the Railway volume at /app/data mounts root-owned.
FROM maximhq/bifrost:v1.6.9
USER root
EXPOSE 8080
